.TH SLOINFO 1
.SH NAME
sloinfo \- display information about compiled openRender shaders
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsloinfo\fR [ name.slo | name.rslo ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Sloinfo
scans the specified compiled shader files and displays information about them.
It auto-detects the file format from the first two bytes: files beginning with
\fB0x42 0x43\fR (LLVM bitcode magic) are parsed as \fB.slo\fR LLVM bitcode shaders;
all other files are parsed as \fB.rslo\fR interpreter bytecode shaders.
If no files are specified,
.I sloinfo
displays information about all compiled shaders (\fB.slo\fR and \fB.rslo\fR) in the
current directory.
.PP
The information displayed for each shader is:
.IP \(bu 4
the shader's name,
.IP \(bu 4
the shader's type (surface, light, displacement, volume, imager, transformation),
.IP \(bu 4
the shader's parameters, their types, storage class, and default values.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
Be verbose.
.TP
.B \-h
Print a short help message.
.TP
.B \-version
Print version information.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENRENDER_SHADERPATH
A colon-separated list of directories to search for shaders when no files are specified.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
orender(1), oshader(1), rsloinfo(1)
.SH AUTHOR
The openRender Team.
.SH NOTES
.I sloinfo
is part of the openRender project.
.I rsloinfo
is a compatibility symlink pointing to
.I sloinfo.
